  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Stella Blue** (2 reviews): The performance of this song was considered nice by the reviewer; The transition from Not Fade Away to this song is quite pretty [4][5]\n- **The Promised Land** (1 review): Played loosely and carefree, though Bobby frequently forgot the lyrics [3]\n- **Sugaree** (1 review): Described as sounding tired and messy during the performance [3]\n- **Not Fade Away** (1 review): A nice jam transitioned into the song, which the listener enjoyed [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Might as Well**: back after 112 archived shows (466 days) [10]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1979-02-11.155704.aud.remaster.acetboy.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 154 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n- **gd79-02-11.naks.vernon.16468.sbeok.shnf**: audience recording; 20 songs; 154 min; rated 2.6/5 by 5 [2]. Said about its sound: The recording is noted as cloudy, which hinders the listening experience; The audio is a bit murky but clearer than many pre-digital tapes; Minimal high end and hard-to-hear drums, but main instruments are clear [3][5][6][7]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- An encore performance of U.S. Blues was included [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1979-02-11.155704.aud.remaster.acetboy.flac16**: transferred by Remaster by acetboy; source: This remaster was created from the shn #16468 files. [1]. Also: Remaster created from share 16468, correcting phase inversion to reveal stereo [1]\n- **gd79-02-11.naks.vernon.16468.sbeok.shnf**: source: Audience Recording: 3 Nak CM-300's [2]. Also: Recorded with three Nak CM-300s into a Nak 550; Transferred via Raoul Duke and encoded by Matt Vernon [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by LiveGRATEFUL.net: [Grateful Dead 1979-02-11 Sun Kiel Auditorium, St. Louis, MO](https://www.livegrateful.net/post/1118828765214/grateful-dead-february-11-1979-kiel) [11]",
